Subject: Stamp the release label into the bootstrap Bazel jar
Description: compile.sh builds the stage-1 Bazel without build-data.properties, so native.bazel_version is empty. bazel_features, loaded by the MLMD WORKSPACE, reads an empty version as a development build newer than any release and loads Bazel 8 APIs, failing with "name 'macro' is not defined". Writing build.label from EMBED_LABEL makes the bootstrapped binary report its real 7.x version.
Origin: DHI-internal (musl build of Bazel for the alpine leaf)
Base-Tree: tarball https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/releases/download/7.7.2/bazel-7.7.2-dist.zip sha256:f40c88b52da292746b6ccf742a0e3f0897a7e4ac24d0143b860f1857f220d5ec
Forwarded: not-needed (upstream release binaries are built by Bazel itself, not by compile.sh)
Drop-When: never: no Bazel 7.x compile.sh writes build-data.properties; re-check when the 7.x track moves
Verify: cmd `bazel --batch version` expect "Build label: 7.7.2"

--- a/scripts/bootstrap/compile.sh
+++ b/scripts/bootstrap/compile.sh
@@ -315,6 +315,10 @@
   # Set up @maven properly
   cp derived/maven/BUILD.vendor derived/maven/BUILD
 
+  # Without build data the bootstrap binary reports an empty version, which
+  # bazel_features treats as newer than any release (it then loads Bazel 8 APIs).
+  echo "build.label=${EMBED_LABEL%% *}" > "${OUTPUT_DIR}/classes/build-data.properties"
+
   create_deploy_jar "libblaze" "com.google.devtools.build.lib.bazel.Bazel" \
       ${OUTPUT_DIR}
 fi
